From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] darwin: build for iOS and tvOS

libbluray 1.4.0 does not build for iOS or tvOS. On every Darwin host its
meson build requires the DiskArbitration framework, and the Darwin mount
helper includes a DiskArbitration header, but only the macOS SDK has
DiskArbitration. On tvOS, vfork and execl, which the macOS Java home
lookup uses to run /usr/libexec/java_home, are unavailable.

Link DiskArbitration only when the SDK has it (HAVE_DISKARBITRATION).
Without it, the mount point lookup for a block device is not performed
and finds no mount point, so mount_get_mountpoint() returns the device
path as it does when DiskArbitration finds none; only CoreFoundation is
linked. On iOS and tvOS (TARGET_OS_IPHONE), the Java home lookup never
runs the helper process and behaves as if vfork had failed: it logs
"vfork failed" and returns no Java home, so libbluray falls back to its
other ways of finding a Java runtime. macOS builds are unchanged.

Licence: this patch is part of Vivid's Lucid Engine patch series for
libbluray. Like the files it modifies, it is free software; you can
redistribute it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU Lesser
